From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mobilizon-patched <noreply@github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 07:54:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add opt-in restricted and locked profiles

MOBILIZON_INSTANCE_RESTRICT_PROFILES=true (config :mobilizon, :instance,
restrict_profiles: true) limits every non-admin account to one profile,
whatever the login method (local, LDAP, OAuth).

MOBILIZON_INSTANCE_LOCK_PROFILES=true (lock_profiles: true) goes further: the
profile username and display name both come from the part of the account
email before the @ (lowercased, other characters than a-z0-9_ become _).
The profile is created on the first login, its display name can't be changed
and is reset to the username on every login. A local signup whose username
is already taken is refused, and an LDAP or OAuth login whose username is
taken fails.

Administrators are exempt from both. Both default to false, so the image
behaves like upstream until enabled.

The production Docker build uses npm ci with the committed package-lock.json
(no longer excluded by .dockerignore), as npm install re-resolves the
dependency tree and currently fails.

The auth controller fetches cookies, so the generic OIDC strategy
(ueberauth_oidcc) can read its state cookie on the callback instead of
crashing.

The login page shows a button for every OAuth provider that has a label in
the config, not only for the ids in its built-in list, so a generic OpenID
Connect provider can use any id, such as oidc.
